      "level": 2,
      "content": "THE PREAMBLE OF THE INDIAN CONSTITUTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The key keywords defining the Indian polity in the Preamble are Sovereign, Socialist, Secular, Democratic, and Republic.",
        "The core objectives of the Constitution set out in the Preamble are Justice, Liberty, Equality, and Fraternity.",
        "The chapter covers the historical background, original text, and amendments made to the Preamble.",
        "It details various Supreme Court judgments evaluating whether the Preamble forms part of the Basic Structure of the Constitution."
      ],
      "id": "hl6605q"
